<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  SPEC.md 4.4d - Dragon Aspect, the last of the fourteen core shouts.

  The three words do this, as settled with the user on 2026-07-29:

    Mul           armour, and heavier melee blows
    Mul Qah       armour x4, plus fire and frost resistance
    Mul Qah Diiv  armour x6, plus reduced shout cooldown, plus the Ancient Dragonborn

  Two of those needed checking against the real game before any number was chosen, and both
  came back differently from how they were asked for. See COMPAT.md section 10.

    - "increased melee damage" has NO Core stat. MeleeDamageFactor is defined in
      Biotech/Defs/Stats/Stats_Pawns_Combat.xml, and CLAUDE.md invariant 5 says the mod must
      run without Biotech. It is applied by a Harmony patch on the melee damage path instead,
      gated on the registry like every other combat-path patch here.

    - "frost resistance" has no stat at all. RimWorld of Magic files its frost damage under
      the HEAT armour category (5 of its 7 frost defs), Dragon's Descent and RWoM's Iceshard
      use Sharp, The Profaned uses Blunt - so ArmorRating_Heat/Sharp/Blunt between them cover
      every frost source in the modlist. Vanilla's own Frostbite has no armour category and
      cannot be resisted by armour at all, only by Insulation_Cold, which is why the hediff
      carries insulation as well.

  Costs and cooldowns: this is the showpiece, and SPEC 4.4d asks for a "once-per-fight feel".
  It is priced just under Storm Call (10/16/24) but with by far the longest cooldown of any
  shout - a minute at one word, two minutes at three.
-->
<Defs>

  <Dovahkiin.WordOfPowerDef>
    <defName>Dovahkiin_Word_Mul</defName>
    <label>Mul</label>
    <word>Mul</word>
    <meaning>Strength</meaning>
  </Dovahkiin.WordOfPowerDef>
  <Dovahkiin.WordOfPowerDef>
    <defName>Dovahkiin_Word_Qah</defName>
    <label>Qah</label>
    <word>Qah</word>
    <meaning>Armor</meaning>
  </Dovahkiin.WordOfPowerDef>
  <Dovahkiin.WordOfPowerDef>
    <defName>Dovahkiin_Word_Diiv</defName>
    <label>Diiv</label>
    <word>Diiv</word>
    <meaning>Wyrm</meaning>
  </Dovahkiin.WordOfPowerDef>

  <Dovahkiin.ShoutDef>
    <defName>Dovahkiin_Shout_DragonAspect</defName>
    <label>Dragon Aspect</label>
    <description>The oldest and mightiest of Shouts. Spectral dragon armour closes over you, and for a while you are less a mortal than a wyrm wearing one.</description>
    <words>
      <li>Dovahkiin_Word_Mul</li>
      <li>Dovahkiin_Word_Qah</li>
      <li>Dovahkiin_Word_Diiv</li>
    </words>
    <abilitiesByLevel>
      <li>Dovahkiin_Ability_DragonAspect_1</li>
      <li>Dovahkiin_Ability_DragonAspect_2</li>
      <li>Dovahkiin_Ability_DragonAspect_3</li>
    </abilitiesByLevel>
    <!--
      TES5's once-per-day power, not a combat shout. Three numbers carry that, and they are
      deliberately in TWO different places:

        thuumCostByLevel      0  - it costs no Voice at all
        cooldownTicksByLevel  60 - the SHARED cooldown, one second
        AbilityDef cooldownTicksRange 60000 - Dragon Aspect's OWN cooldown, a full day

      The distinction matters. cooldownTicksByLevel here is the "general shouting" lockout
      that blocks EVERY other shout (SPEC.md 4.2 - one shared cooldown, whose length is set
      by the shout just used). Putting a day into it would silence the Thu'um entirely for
      that day, which is not what a once-per-day power means. So the shared lockout is
      almost nothing, and the day-long wait lives on the AbilityDef, where vanilla's own
      per-ability cooldown enforces it.

      A cost of zero is safe: Need_Thuum.CanAfford(0) is CurLevel >= 0, always true, and
      TrySpend(0) subtracts nothing. No division anywhere on that path.
    -->
    <thuumCostByLevel><li>0</li><li>0</li><li>0</li></thuumCostByLevel>
    <cooldownTicksByLevel><li>60</li><li>60</li><li>60</li></cooldownTicksByLevel>
    <!-- SPEC.md 4.5 / 4.6: dragons and draugr get only Force, Fire and Frost. Never this. -->
    <availableToDragons>false</availableToDragons>
    <availableToUndead>false</availableToUndead>
  </Dovahkiin.ShoutDef>

</Defs>
